---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Culprit';
const description =
  'Culprit is being built privacy-first. Our full privacy policy publishes here before launch. Data questions: privacy@getculprit.app.';
---

<Page
  title={title}
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  description={description}
  index={false}
  updated="Draft in progress — the full policy publishes here before Culprit launches."
>
  <p>
    Culprit is being built privacy-first, and our full privacy policy is being
    finalized. It will be published on this page before Culprit is available to
    download.
  </p>

  <h2>What it will cover</h2>
  <p>When it lands, the policy will explain, in plain language:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>what Culprit collects, and why;</li>
    <li>the services that help process it, and what each one sees;</li>
    <li>how long information is kept;</li>
    <li>how to delete your account and all of its data, at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The waitlist</h2>
  <p>
    If you enter your email on this page, we use it for one thing: to send you a
    single email when Culprit reaches the App Store. No newsletter, no ad
    targeting, and we don&rsquo;t sell or share it. Your address is stored on our
    infrastructure (Cloudflare) and, if it helps us gauge interest, the country
    your request came from. Ask us to remove you at any time — email
    <a href="mailto:support@getculprit.app">support@getculprit.app</a> and it&rsquo;s
    gone.
  </p>

  <h2>About this website</h2>
  <p>
    This site, getculprit.app, is a static page. It doesn&rsquo;t set
    advertising cookies, and it doesn&rsquo;t sell your data. If we later add
    analytics, we&rsquo;ll use a cookieless, privacy-respecting option and name
    it here.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions in the meantime</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:privacy@getculprit.app">privacy@getculprit.app</a> with
    any question about your data and we&rsquo;ll reply.
  </p>
</Page>
